From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: ImageBrush and TileBrush

Windows.UI.Xaml.Media.ImageBrush and TileBrush were missing. OneDrive's last setup page (after "Sync your files to this PC") makes an ImageBrush; the stowed REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG failed OneDrive fast and it ended without a word. They are now there (activatable ImageBrush, composable TileBrush, their statics, markup and compiled markup), with AlignmentX/AlignmentY/Stretch and ImageSource; ImageOpened is raised when a source with its pixels is set. An ImageBrush fills a Panel's, Border's or Control's Background and a Rectangle's or Ellipse's Fill: the image placed by Stretch and the alignments, inside the area (rounded corners and the ellipse as a mask).
---
